      "value": "@{5f7d7122a316926b4614afc1|full_name}: That you can only call it for the localPlayer, not for other players. That's why it's a self-report API. The best way to do this would be to include random network events in known public worlds that look harmless but identify the client as having said mods when they are received from the servers. You just need to randomize it to be undetectable, it needs to look like part of the world / normal client behaviour. This can easily be done with Udon itself btw., we do it already in our world, we just can't do anything meaningful based on that information as of now.",
      "viewerReactions": null
