      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5f2dc3d9b923f7086bb0a2b5|full_name}: Anti-Teleport & No-Udon mods are so common that simply teleporting them somewhere isn't solving this issue. Easy to detect, but hard to stop them from messing up a world. Also removing them from a single world isn't helping the platform. Although this canny is about so much more, not only about the mod users, but also about limiting their abilities to mess with other people by adding authentication to Udon events and basic encryption classes. And in the end, if VRChat wanted to, they could easily add code to the client to mass-remove client users with certain malicious mods to set an example if they wanted to.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
