      "value": "@{5f3287055bc2dc276e0f1630|full_name}: There is still the issue of malicious world creators abusing the api to target players (just to name one issue with this). The fact that the average world creator isn't as shitty of a person as the average hacker doesn't make this watertight. But i am definitely in favor of some of these suggetions, like kicking the local player. About the people disabling Udon btw, theres a pretty easy solution to that: Just don't load anything in the world unless its enabled, for example by having the spawn be an area with just an invisible collider on the floor that teleports people somewhere else (to the \"actual\" spawn). I'm doing similar stuff to that for optimisation reasons, but it could easily be used to make a world unplayable for people who have Udon disabled.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
