      "value": "@{601cc0baf76d3163c5fe2aa3|full_name}: Yes, that should be a secret \"API\" that VRChat implements in some known worlds with their creators together, or even without them. The point is to do some effort to reduce those malicious mods. The thing is, VRChat could detect those with a single path exists check in their client, then collect those users and mass-delete them to set an example. Would it solve the problem forever? No, but it would show that they are doing something against it which is currently not the case, hence this canny.\nRegarding your suggestion: People toggle Udon on/off on demand after they spawn, so loading the world in Udon doesn't solve this issue at all unfortunately.",
      "viewerReactions": null
